      "boundary_basis": "multi_source_ecological_context",
      "boundary_scope_note": "This is the ecological waterbody entity, distinct from the statutory aquatic preserve and the Biscayne National Park boundary. Its polygon must be assembled from authoritative shoreline, hydrographic, and tidal-connection evidence. NOAA Harbour ENC also contains 37 charted Biscayne Bay named-water polygons across 17 ENC cells. These are chart-cell fragments, not a complete ecological or statutory boundary. A first geometric topology precheck is complete: the union has two disconnected components, one a very small isolated fragment. Full boundary reconciliation remains pending. Original chart fragments are persisted individually; no dissolved or complete boundary is promoted. The NOAA charted named-water union was overlaid against FDEP Biscayne Bay Aquatic Preserve OBJECTID 43; the substantial mismatch confirms that these are different source concepts and neither is a complete ecological bay boundary. NOAA NGS shoreline projects FL1808C-TB-N (GC12023) and FL1808A-TB-N (GC12021) are identified as high-accuracy MHW/MLLW shoreline candidates but have not yet been retrieved. NOAA NGS metadata shows an apparent latitude interval between FL1808A and FL1808C project extents; because those extents are data-management rectangles, this is a coverage question to inspect, not a confirmed shoreline gap. FL1603A Convoy Point is local supplemental coverage; FL1934E is historical only.",
